 "preferred_name": "Generalized linear model",
 "kind": "method",
 "definition": "A statistical model that extends linear regression to outcomes that are not normally distributed by using a link function.",
 "description": {
  "text": "A flexible generalization of ordinary linear regression in statistics. It lets the linear model relate to the response variable through a link function, and lets each measurement's variance depend on its predicted value. It was formulated by John Nelder and Robert Wedderburn.",
